Project files for Visual C are distributed with the NetHack source code.

>But really, what is causing this error?  

Windows looks in a certain set of directories to find commands you type
on the command line. For example, common Windows commands such as xcopy,
cacls or net are programs in c:\windows\system32 (%WINDIR%\system32, to
be exact). This set of directories is set in the environment variable
PATH. Apparently, the path where the programs of mingw reside has not
been added to this list.

However, amending the path might not be enough to ensure correct
compilation, because mingw might need other environment variables to work
correctly; someone familiar with mingw has to check this.

